{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves","id":517679,"title":"A City Lacking Werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-17T23:08:03-07:00","id":517679,"title":"A City Lacking Werewolves","content":"Curious about other people's perspectives. Take one small city of 1.6 million people. Only small isolated wounds here and there. Nothing massively nasty in the spirit world. Let's say, though, that another supernatural group managed to cull a number of the fractious werewolves which were always in small numbers in a city which had already had large tracts of gauntlet unpatrolled. What would you have happen to the city? And how noticeable would it be? Just curious in terms of how important other GMs make the werewolves to the health of their areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T23:28:35-07:00","id":517704,"title":"","content":"Depends on the splats inhabiting the city tbh. If there were a lot of mages they could theoretically shape the cities shadow to their liking. I'm not really sure how other supernaturals would handle things though. Chances are as long as no really powerful spirit was influencing things behind the scene things would stay relatively the same. I mean it isn't like werewolves are everywhere, and the places without werewolves probably aren't all collapsing in on themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-18-2015, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T00:14:55-07:00","id":517720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves#post517679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious about other people's perspectives. Take one small city of 1.6 million people. Only small isolated wounds here and there. Nothing massively nasty in the spirit world. Let's say, though, that another supernatural group managed to cull a number of the fractious werewolves which were always in small numbers in a city which had already had large tracts of gauntlet unpatrolled. What would you have happen to the city? And how noticeable would it be? Just curious in terms of how important other GMs make the werewolves to the health of their areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter Cells would start to spring up to deal with the Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:39:21-07:00","id":518209,"title":"","content":"This should be a fun thread.<br /> <br /> 'Nor had the years been pleasant for the city. The Beshilu left pestilence in their wake, spreading sickness and decay. Thousands had died from what human scientists had labeled a resistant outbreak of tuberculosis. Panic and disorder followed the disease's spread, eventually forcing the governor to declare martial law and send in the National Guard to restore order.'<br /> <br /> That's from the core book, and it's while there are werewolves in the city and they're actively on a sacred hunt for the Beshilu, the rat hosts.<br /> <br /> Wherever you don't have werewolves culling things you have a potential for disaster. Especially since some of their antagonists are aware of a larger picture and can take advantage of things like a lack of werewolves in a city.<br /> <br /> Obviously you can go the easy route and say nothing happens. But between the myriad of werewolf antagonists, even cutting out other werewolves, you can have extremely nasty stuff go down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T04:12:24-07:00","id":519357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves#post517679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take one small city of 1.6 million people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little Sidestep: &quot;Small city&quot;? It's like the capitol of Poland, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warsaw\" target=\"_blank\">Warsaw</a> ( circa 1.7 million citizens ). I would say that this big place would have at least a dozen of various packs or other supernatural groups ( and few of them would be classical antagonists ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T21:25:19-07:00","id":522910,"title":"","content":"Once the spirits know that no one is actively keeping an eye on them, some will start to overstep their bounds. At first, nobody is likely to notice except the statisticians. Emotions run unnaturally high, leading to higher rates of suicide, murder, abuse, and all manner of lesser crimes. It's not all bad, though; marriage rates probably go up (though so too might divorces), as do births. Since there are far fewer consequences to deal with, spirits who interfere with the physical world can gain a major advantage over their rivals, and more denizens of the shadow join them in order to compete.<br /> <br /> Before long, all the locals start to realize that there's something wrong with the city. Most won't have any explanation for it, but they might leave town all the same, muttering about what a nice neighborhood it used to be before things started to go downhill. Those who stay will only add to the spiritual decay of the city, as their nameless fears and vague anxieties feed the worst kinds of spirits.<br /> <br /> More and more, observant citizens will start to encounter things that shake their very perceptions of reality. A pathologist at a major local hospital finds himself sleeping less and less as he obsesses over a disease that he can't even classify, but which seems to be spreading through the area with little rhyme or reason. A seasoned police detective is forced to fire on a young man wanted in connection with a string of brutal murders, whose manic smile doesn't so much as waver as the bullets tear his organs to pieces. A single mother grapples with the horrifying realization that the <i>thing</i> sleeping in her daughter's bed and wearing her clothes isn't her little girl at all. A couple of drunk college kids accidentally stumble across a verge, and only one manages to find the way out again.<br /> <br /> Some of these people will no doubt become hunters, and existing compacts and conspiracies with some knowledge of the spirit world are likely to become very interested in the city as the situation develops. Without the Uratha's innate ability to see and interact with the denizens of Twilight, however, they'll probably only be able to address the most obvious symptoms of the problem.<br /> <br /> Given enough time, the city will probably start to die. Businesses will go belly up or relocate to greener pastures. People with the means will abandon their homes and move away, as the city climbs lists of the most dangerous and depressing places to live. Barring some massive disaster, the husk that remains can probably continue to linger on indefinitely, inhabited by the desperate and those who prey on them, but it's unlikely to ever recover unless someone comes by with the means and the desire to sort out the mess in the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 05-21-2015, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T22:14:01-07:00","id":522929,"title":"","content":"I'd personally say that nature abhors a vacuum and that something else would step in to fill the void. A powerful spirit might step in and begin enforcing its own set of rules and laws locally, to stop werewolves from hopefully showing up. A cabal of Thrysus mages might take it upon themselves to start trying to keep the city's shadow in line. Whatever it was, I would say that something would try and fill the role (even if it is a young pack showing up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T00:12:08-07:00","id":522982,"title":"","content":"werewolves aren't present in the most of the world, it's still standing. I would say that there would be a short period of struggle and than something else would fill the role. Maybe a cabal of mages, a powerful spirit, something like that. World isn't a glass castle hanging on the presence of werewolves to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T04:13:44-07:00","id":523084,"title":"","content":"The city decides not to host the winter olympics after having already won the right to.<br /> <br /> More seriously I've never been to Denver but despite the Idigam, there certainly seem like worse places to live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:40:40-07:00","id":523471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=522982#post522982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">werewolves aren't present in the most of the world, it's still standing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like where?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> World isn't a glass castle hanging on the presence of werewolves to survive. </div> </div> </div>Isn't it? At least Humanity's part in it?<br /> <br /> So we mentioned the Beshilu, with their virulent diseases. Alternatively you have the Azlu, the spider hosts. With them you get a sort of opposite effect. A dulling of experience, as they thicken the Gauntlet until its impenetrable and no Essence can get through and spirits can't influence or reach the other way. I imagine at the end it would be like that world from Serenity, where everyone just sort of stops and dies. Except there would be spider-webs everywhere, like at the end of that movie where tarantulas took over some town in the South. And of course when new people come to town they're be curious, but the moment they'd separate from the group or slip into a dark alley, one of three things would happen.<br /> <br /> 1. A tiny azlu slips from the Gauntlet at about ear-level and crawls into their brain to take control.<br /> <br /> 2. A swarm of spiders scurry out of the Gauntlet and engulf the person.<br /> <br /> 3. A massive trapdoor in the Gauntlet opens and an azlu the size of a truck grabs them and pulls them in, never to be seen again.<br /> <br /> Azlu strongholds would be pretty creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-21-2015, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:45:24-07:00","id":523476,"title":"","content":"Theoretically left to run amok the azlu and beshilu would cancel each other out. Or at least get into a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:48:12-07:00","id":523480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves#post517679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious about other people's perspectives. Take one small city of 1.6 million people. Only small isolated wounds here and there. Nothing massively nasty in the spirit world. Let's say, though, that another supernatural group managed to cull a number of the fractious werewolves which were always in small numbers in a city which had already had large tracts of gauntlet unpatrolled. What would you have happen to the city? And how noticeable would it be? Just curious in terms of how important other GMs make the werewolves to the health of their areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 word for you: Detroit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:29:40-07:00","id":523514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=523476#post523476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theoretically left to run amok the azlu and beshilu would cancel each other out. Or at least get into a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Providing they were in the same locale, yes. But it's possible for just azlu to take a city and just beshilu to as well.<br /> <br /> Claimed can go either way. In first edition we have examples of Claimed that don't really do anything, though they could upset the dynamic of global political power. The Book of Spirits has Cray, a woman Claimed by a computer spirit who is, essentially, the most powerful computer in the world. If an agent of a government found her it would be pretty easy to bring her into the fold, as she seems pretty obliging, and just use her for whatever purposes said government wanted.<br /> <br /> But you also have the more proactive Claimed. Not everyone manages to be Claimed by an inanimate object, and Chicago introduced the Blister Man as a Fire-Claimed who used their powers to engulf buildings with flames. This was a planned attempt by them to 'rebalance' the city's Shadow, which is altered during the Winter months. Now it's easy to say that fires can just be put out by firemen, but the shift in the balance of the city's essence the Seven Conflagrations, the spirit claiming the Blister Man, or woman, causes a series of chain reactions throughout the Hisil. Spirits that shouldn't be around start forcing their way into loci, the city starts obtaining more fire and water resonance, the choirs of each seemingly itching for a fight. Fear spirits are in abundance. And strangely enough, wherever the Claimed sets a fire, Wounds appear immediately.<br /> <br /> As an interesting side note, the Blister Man is probably the first in-game example of a Hive-claimed, being a single person inhabited by seven spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-21-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T19:50:21-07:00","id":523862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=522982#post522982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">World isn't a glass castle hanging on the presence of werewolves to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno; neither Werewolf nor Mage seem all that shy about suggesting the possibility of apocalyptic scenarios, at least on a regional scale. The main difference is that mages seem more likely to be the ones inadvertently <i>causing</i> the apocalypse. :P<br /> <br /> Further, if the world would be just fine without the Uratha, it casts them in a very different light. Instead of violent religious zealots fighting to protect the balance of the world, they become just plain violent religious zealots. Which is fine, I suppose, if that's the way your group wants to play it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T21:03:02-07:00","id":523960,"title":"","content":"Unless something has changed and I missed it, the spirit world (shadow) is ruled by spirit courts with those reflecting the environment standing dominant, that means nature spirits in the wilderness, sea spirits in deep water and city spirits in the cities. Spirits protect their territory and their food source and that means city spirits will work to protect their city, big problems would normally only happen if something upsets the balance. The rats and spiders are unique in that they work from the material side of the fence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T00:29:51-07:00","id":525204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=523471#post523471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like where?<br /> <br /> Isn't it? At least Humanity's part in it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Africa. Polynesia, China, Arctica/Antarctica, Japan, Middle East, India, everywhere In the open sea.<br /> <br /> 2) Nope, nobody really cares about a small staff. But in case of the serious problems, higher powers [shadow gods, ascended mages, etc] arrange for intervention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T01:49:38-07:00","id":525292,"title":"","content":"This would actually explain all those weirdass deep-sea fish. They're Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T07:56:06-07:00","id":525456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=525204#post525204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Africa. Polynesia, China, Arctica/Antarctica, Japan, Middle East, India</div> </div> </div> </div>There are confirmed werewolves in over half of these locations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T08:18:28-07:00","id":525466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=525456#post525456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are confirmed werewolves in over half of these locations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know at least two settings in WtF2 are set in the Middle East and Japan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T08:46:52-07:00","id":525501,"title":"","content":"Left unchecked, Antarctica is the domain of the Great Pyn-Guu, Lord of the Wastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T09:07:43-07:00","id":525516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=525292#post525292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would actually explain all those weirdass deep-sea fish. They're Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kraken was a giant squid who was Claimed by a spirit of destruction/hunger? Headcanon <i>accepted</i><br /> <br /> (And now to do a Werewolf version of <i>Jaws</i>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T11:00:24-07:00","id":525626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=525204#post525204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Africa. Polynesia, China, Arctica/Antarctica, Japan, Middle East, India, everywhere In the open sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition, at least, we have werewolves in all of those. Providing lodges haven't disappeared and all the fiction isn't null, we still do. Also as pointed out there's examples of werewolves in some of those places in second edition. You might be thinking wolves, but the existence or nonexistence of wolves has no relation to the existence of werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Nope, nobody really cares about a small staff. But in case of the serious problems, higher powers [shadow gods, ascended mages, etc] arrange for intervention. </div> </div> </div>Except Shadow Gods and ascended mages might be the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T11:10:01-07:00","id":525630,"title":"","content":"I've occasionally wondered if the idea that wolves never went extinct in Britain in the World of Darkness would be too big a change to casually slip in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T11:17:20-07:00","id":525633,"title":"","content":"I'd wonder if all wolves went extinct if the 'wolf' form of werewolves would change to some other predator, like a great cat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T23:00:58-07:00","id":526422,"title":"","content":"In first edition (not sure which book) it was suggested that werewolves' wolf-like forms would tend to naturally shift to better blend in with the local wildlife. In areas with no wolves, they tended to look somewhat more doglike, either resembling large relatively wolf-like breeds of domestic dog or a local variety of wild or feral dog. As I recall, some of the werewolves in Africa and the Middle East had urhan forms that could be mistaken for hyenas, even though hyenas aren't actually canids at all.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, there explicitly <i>were</i> werewolves in Africa, and the Uratha have always been somewhat associated with Sumeria in what is now the Middle East. I can't point to a specific reference, but as I recall in first edition the Pure had a strong presence in Hawaii, and possibly other parts of Polynesia. The second edition core book has Basra in Iraq and Tokyo in Japan as example settings for a Forsaken game. As for China, India, and the Arctic, all of those regions have or historically had native populations of wolves (not to mention humans), so it would be kind of strange if there were no werewolves.<br /> <br /> The relative lack of living things, and particularly of humans (who are the biggest producers of essence) means that Antarctica probably has few spirits of much power or ambition. Most of its elemental and geographical spirits are probably dormant, except perhaps in areas where humans have had a direct impact on the landscape. Still, it would probably be a perfect place for Idigam or other weird spirits to lie low and plot world domination, or whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T23:09:04-07:00","id":526428,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the books make it clear that wherever there's humans, there's werewolves. While there's probably slighter mentions of them across the books, Africa is the homeground of the Lodge of the Hundred Days, Polynesian people often find themselves heading towards Antarctica to join the Lodge of the Lake, including the 'signature' Lodge of the Lake character, Frostbite, who is was driven from New Zealand by a pack of Predator Kings. China has a historical entry in the Against the Pure detailing the battles of werewolves during the Yellow Turban Rebellion, Japan has the Lodge of the Hungry Ghosts, Middle East has Basra, the opening fiction to Lodges: the Splintered is about a werewolf in Bangladesh, and the Kshatriyas is a lodge of Storm Lords in India, rounding up them all, the open sea has the Lodge of the Maelstrom, as well as other sea-going packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T22:57:29-07:00","id":530706,"title":"","content":"So, yeah, it's been established that werewolves can be, and often are, pretty much everywhere in the world. &quot;mages will take care of it&quot;. Is only something that can even be possibly presumed if you are running a cross over game, as it isn't established in base Werewolf that sorcerers of that kind of power even exist in a given setting.<br /> <br /> I think that in a city with no werewolves, you very much risk the city turning into the type of dystopia described in a lot of the legends of Urfarah, a particular spirit court manages to establish a whole lot of power, probably of a very malevolent resonance, as those are the most powerful and enduring types within the shadow, and then reaching into the physical world to enslave humanity and turn them into meat puppets to be claimed, and factories for their favored essence. The entire city could wind up quarantined by government forces due to too much spooky stuff that human governments just aren't equipped to handle. Imagine if a court of technology went about enslaving engineers and technicians to create devices of the spirits own design, attacking the APCs of government responses and scrambling communications going in or out. It could get gnarly in a lot of different ways depending on the particular court that rose to power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:47:17-07:00","id":531008,"title":"","content":"Mages have no vested interest in preserving the spiritual ecosystem. The only thing that you can really be sure of when they're involved is that they'll wanna see what's going on, not necessarily fix it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T06:14:39-07:00","id":534266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=531008#post531008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages have no vested interest in preserving the spiritual ecosystem. The only thing that you can really be sure of when they're involved is that they'll wanna see what's going on, not necessarily fix it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily true. If spirits were mucking up the things they liked mages would probably do something about it. They likely wouldn't care that much about the specifics, but if things started falling apart they'd definitely take measures to stop it assuming things this side of the gauntlet took a turn for the worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:05:12-07:00","id":536199,"title":"","content":"Its an interesting thought experiment as well. Because if everything gets along fine without werewolves, well that makes werewolves a sort of defunct species. &quot;Hey pack, lets go hunt beshilu!&quot; &quot;Nah the spirit world will solve itself.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T18:06:00-07:00","id":536297,"title":"","content":"That would be true if their job was to save the spirit world, but they're spirits of the hunt. Their job is to hunt. The Forsaken just protect the border to honor Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> As long as a living or dead thing or concept exists to hunt, werewolves have a place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=534266#post534266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If spirits were mucking up the things they liked mages would probably do something about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If spirits were mucking up the things mages liked, they'd have a vested interest. Leetsepeak was pointing out that on their own, they have no responsibility to the Hisil. But even providing some mages saw a problem, decided they had to do something about it, and had the ability to, considering their foreign nature to the spirit, it's likely whatever they did would not exactly cure it. They could probably institute a fine bandaid but after a while you might have a problem like Australia did with the introduction of cane toads, then red foxes, and rabbits and cats and on and on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-01-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T18:18:39-07:00","id":536305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=531008#post531008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages have no vested interest in preserving the spiritual ecosystem. The only thing that you can really be sure of when they're involved is that they'll wanna see what's going on, not necessarily fix it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrast with taking advantage of the lack of spiritual balance for their personal knowledge/gain, is completely possible as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T19:14:44-07:00","id":536381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=536305#post536305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrast with taking advantage of the lack of spiritual balance for their personal knowledge/gain, is completely possible as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to imagine some of the Predator Kings and other more self-centered of werewolves would do that too. Why stop a small spirit making trouble, when if you wait you can call a hunt on a far more powerful spirit?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T19:49:44-07:00","id":536403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=536381#post536381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to imagine some of the Predator Kings and other more self-centered of werewolves would do that too. Why stop a small spirit making trouble, when if you wait you can call a hunt on a far more powerful spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the whole premise behind Balehounds. The Pure are more &quot;Spirits will spirit&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T04:00:19-07:00","id":536785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=536297#post536297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be true if their job was to save the spirit world, but they're spirits of the hunt. Their job is to hunt. The Forsaken just protect the border to honor Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> As long as a living or dead thing or concept exists to hunt, werewolves have a place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If spirits were mucking up the things mages liked, they'd have a vested interest. Leetsepeak was pointing out that on their own, they have no responsibility to the Hisil. But even providing some mages saw a problem, decided they had to do something about it, and had the ability to, considering their foreign nature to the spirit, it's likely whatever they did would not exactly cure it. They could probably institute a fine bandaid but after a while you might have a problem like Australia did with the introduction of cane toads, then red foxes, and rabbits and cats and on and on.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there are mages or people mages care about in the city, which I would assume is true given that they were even brought up as a possibility, then if this side of the gauntlet goes to shit they'd have a vested interest in the situation. If whatever was going on in the shadow has no meaningful effect on whats happening on the material side of things then sure, the mages likely wouldn't care, but then again there really wouldn't be much that needed to be caring about.<br /> <br /> So assuming there is a problem and there are mages there, they'll obviously notice something is up because that's what mages do. If the problem is meaningful enough to effect more than a small handful of people that none of them care about they might not care enough to act, but anything presenting a big enough threat to honestly make a difference on a city level is obviously going to be acted upon or taken advantage of, if only to preserve their own interest. So long story short, at least when it comes to a place housing even a mentionable number of mages, chances are things aren't going to be allowed to spiral too out of control.<br /> <br /> Though as I mentioned before, this is only concerning mages, where 1/5th of their population has access to powers dealing with spirits and the like. I don't really know how well vampires, changelings, etc. would handle the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T05:11:36-07:00","id":536815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves?p=536785#post536785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there are mages or people mages care about in the city, which I would assume is true given that they were even brought up as a possibility, then if this side of the gauntlet goes to shit they'd have a vested interest in the situation. If whatever was going on in the shadow has no meaningful effect on whats happening on the material side of things then sure, the mages likely wouldn't care, but then again there really wouldn't be much that needed to be caring about.<br /> <br /> So assuming there is a problem and there are mages there, they'll obviously notice something is up because that's what mages do. If the problem is meaningful enough to effect more than a small handful of people that none of them care about they might not care enough to act, but anything presenting a big enough threat to honestly make a difference on a city level is obviously going to be acted upon or taken advantage of, if only to preserve their own interest. So long story short, at least when it comes to a place housing even a mentionable number of mages, chances are things aren't going to be allowed to spiral too out of control.<br /> <br /> Though as I mentioned before, this is only concerning mages, where 1/5th of their population has access to powers dealing with spirits and the like. I don't really know how well vampires, changelings, etc. would handle the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what I think too. If your house is on fire you are gonna try to save it, even if that's not you job. Also at least 20% of them have access to spirit arcana, non-thyrsus also practice it. Other splats would have very big problems, most have the very rudimentary powers to deal with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T00:07:11-07:00","id":549833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/517679-a-city-lacking-werewolves#post517679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious about other people's perspectives. Take one small city of 1.6 million people. Only small isolated wounds here and there. Nothing massively nasty in the spirit world. Let's say, though, that another supernatural group managed to cull a number of the fractious werewolves which were always in small numbers in a city which had already had large tracts of gauntlet unpatrolled. What would you have happen to the city? And how noticeable would it be? Just curious in terms of how important other GMs make the werewolves to the health of their areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Chronicle is set in a New York that hasn't seen a permanent pack of wolves for ten years. I cheated and wiped the Hisil too. But I only did that after I considered the ramifications of not having a single pack in NYC for that long.<br /> <br /> Spirit Resonance<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> First any human city will generate a metric fuck ton of Essence. And most of it will come from the most emotionally charged events and actions in the city. In Nwod terms this is certainly murders, rapes, riots, and extreme violent accidents. Not much good happens among Men anymore. What rare celebrations exist are fleeting.<br /> This means the most abundant essence other than that of raw \u2018city\u2019 resonance is violence, hate, and pain. Meaning that most conceptual choirs are ruled by it. Wolf pack naturally compete with this resonance. They hunt it down balance out their own turf. No one likes sleeping on a blood soaked mattress made of knives. Least of all wolves.<br /> SO without packs it only made sense the city would fall apart through the feed-back loop of Hisil to Material to Hisil. I couldn\u2019t let that be. But that is least of the city\u2019s many dooms. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Ridden<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Next come the Ridden. Spirits that reach out (perhaps because the city\u2019s Hisil resonance is choked on blood) to find a host to generate their nourishment. Without wolves, the only other Supernatural aware and capable enough to stop Ridden are Mages. So it would make sense that with 80% of the policing force missing the Ridden would grow powerful enough to form pseudo Choirs of their own. A dark image indeed. Dark enough I let them stick around. Don\u2019t tell my players. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Hosts<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ridden may be bad, but the Host take the cake. The Beshilu would eat the city inside out. They largely lack the foresight to manage the human population, and if they did have that foresight it would mean the worst has come true. The Beshilu are organized under a proper Rat King.<br /> The only hope the city would have ironically is an infestation of Azlu. The Spider Hosts would separate the Hisil far enough from the City to allow both to survive longer apart then they would together. Though the separation would mean a host of other issues.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Other SuperNats<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Vamps would hardly understand why the city would be crumbling around them. I\u2019m not up to date on Vamp. But I can only see the Ordu being able stave off the inevitable.<br /> For Mages, the need for Spirit Shamans would mean the Thyrsus Path would have a butt-load of power in the city. I would expect the Stone Book to seize power, likely through the Arrow.<br /> Hunters might figure out some of the problem but their lack of spiritual weight would hamstring their efforts.<br /> Changelings and the rest would just be boned. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> TL;DR:<br /> I opted to just remove the City\u2019s representation altogether and explain it through plot. My wolves threw off the dearth of \u2018city\u2019 when they established their turf boundary with the Hunting Ground Rite. Their turf is \u2018growing\u2019 back quickly while also standing as a juxtaposition to the rest of the empty city.<br /> It beat having to imagine all the horrible calamities the city would otherwise be subject too. Taking back such a broken City didn\u2019t seem appropriate for new-born wolves fresh form their change.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T06:10:44-07:00","id":1495159,"title":"","content":"Resurrecting an old thread, I know... but I felt the need to point out that this premise exists in canon.<br /> <br /> One of the many weird (and tbh, slightly objectionable) decisions that OP made with the suggested Australian setting materials was exactly this premise. Beast: The Primordial pp257-258 puts forward a version of the city of Adelaide (a city of between 1.3 and 1.4 million people) that has - apparently barring a trucker werewolf who passes through periodically - exactly one supernatural residing in it who seems to murder every other supernatural who comes there, and that this has been the case for about 150 years. Has it been the same supernatural the whole time? Who knows. What is that supernatural <i>exactly? </i> Who knows.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, this is the fifth most populated city on the continent and a state capital. It'd be like if Phoenix, Arizona was canonically written to only have one supernatural NPC in it.<br /> <br /> What are the consequences of there canonically being no werewolves in Adelaide? Well... it's just Adelaide. So... I guess the consequences are that there are two vertically stacked metallic spheres at a shopping mall known as &quot;the mall balls&quot; for some reason?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T10:27:03-07:00","id":1495250,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Necromancy is not allowed.</span></b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}